  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "The volume of a cube is $\\frac{8}{27}\\,{\\text{yd}}^{3}.$ Find the length of the edges of the cube.",
  "worked_solution": "Since the volume of a cube is \n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the length of an edge, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns=\\sqrt[3]{V}=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{8}{27}}=\\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the edges is $\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\text{yd}.$",
